3. THE FRONT END'S OUTPUT OVER-VOLTAGE PROTECTION (SNVSAI1D 6.5 p.8; 7.3.11 p.18; 7.1 p.13)
   threshold at FB: VREF + 10 % TYPICAL (no minimum or maximum given), hysteresis 2.5 %; response: 'turns off the gate
   drives' (7.3.11) or 'the high-side drivers' (7.1); either stops the input's energy (Q2 off blocks VIN_RAW). OVP reads FB,
   so it scales with the same divider: the bus trips at 1.10 x its own regulation.
   trip, nominal                                   22.000 V
   trip, VREF maximum and the divider's worst ratio 23.055 V   (INFERRED: TI's 10 % is typical only)
   L1's current in the steady current-limit cycle inside U2's ratings (R12 5 mOhm - 1 %; the CS and CSG pins sit behind
   R150 and R151, 100 Ohm each, where IOFFSET(CS/CSG) up to 19 uA, p.7, moves the threshold by up to 1.9 mV):
     boost mode, peak limit (140 + 1.9) mV:                                     28.67 A
     buck mode at 36.0 V in: valley limit (94 + 1.9) mV = 19.37 A, plus the ripple at the trip (L1 -20 %, 175 kHz)  25.30 A
     buck mode at 55.0 V in: valley limit (94 + 1.9) mV = 19.37 A, plus the ripple at the trip (L1 -20 %, 175 kHz)  28.94 A
     buck mode at 60.0 V in: valley limit (94 + 1.9) mV = 19.37 A, plus the ripple at the trip (L1 -20 %, 175 kHz)  29.51 A
   so buck mode at U2's 60 V sets the steady cycle's peak: 29.51 A; with L1 at +20 % (12 uH) that is 5.23 mJ, which into
   the six bulk parts at -20 % (1.584 mF, ceramics not counted) lifts the bus to 23.198 V.
   THE FIRST ON-TIME (the re-check's n2). In buck mode the LM5176 limits the VALLEY only: the high side 'skips a cycle if
   the sensed voltage does not fall below this threshold' (7.3.5 p.16) and, once on, is 'turned off by the oscillator
   clock signal' (7.3.1 p.14), so the first on-time after a valley crossing can last up to a period. MODEL, a full period
   at U2's 60 V from the valley limit, L1 at -20 %, 175 kHz: 45.76 A; with 12 uH (unsaturated, where L1's Isat is 17.5 A)
   12.57 mJ, and the bus reaches 23.397 V. The bound takes the larger.
   THE BUS'S BOUND: 23.40 V, INFERRED (the typical-only 10 %) with a MODEL energy term. That term weighs little: to put
   the bus at 29.0 V (Q7's 30 V less Q8's VSD) from the trip, L1 would have to deliver 245 mJ, 20 times this figure.
   Response time: TI gives none. None is needed at this scale: at 45.76 A into 1.584 mF the bus rises at most 28.9 V per ms,
   so 0.24 ms of full current past the trip would be needed to reach 30 V (42 cycles at 175 kHz).
   The typical 10 % would have to be wrong by this much before the bus reaches each limit (VREF max, worst ratio, residue):
      24.0 V (80 % of the FETs' 30 V): an OVP 12.9 % over VREF
      26.0 V (the BQ25731's recommended 26 V and ACOV's minimum): an OVP 22.4 % over VREF
      29.0 V (Q7's 30 V, with Q8's VSD): an OVP 36.7 % over VREF
      30.0 V (Q8's 30 V): an OVP 41.5 % over VREF
      32.0 V (the BQ25731's absolute 32 V): an OVP 51.1 % over VREF

4. A LOAD DUMP: THE CHARGER STOPS AT ITS FULL INPUT CURRENT
   The charger's own inductor L2 does not feed VBUS20 when it stops: with Q7 off its current returns through Q8's body
   diode, L2 and Q10 (on, or its body diode) to VBAT. The front end sees a load step and answers with its loop (MODEL:
   crossover 0.71 kHz at its slowest corner, |Zout| 89 mOhm, gen_sch_a.py lines 722 to 724); its CCM stage can sink
   current (SNVSAI1D 7.3.8 p.17). Step dI into the bulk at -20 %: dV = dI / (2 pi fc C), plus L1's energy in the steady
   current-limit cycle (section 3), which overstates what L1 carries at either step (16.2 A at 9 V in, gen_sch_a.py 751):
   6.45 A (Option A(i)'s bound, U3's 6.35 A clamp plus 0.1 A): loop 0.913 V, |Zout| 0.574 V; with 5.23 mJ the peak is 22.023 V
   8.00 A (VBUS20's declared peak): loop 1.132 V, |Zout| 0.712 V; with 5.23 mJ the peak is 22.241 V
   (MODEL; below the OVP trip's 23.055 V, so OVP need not act; whatever the model's error, section 3 caps it at 23.397 V)
   During the dump the charger has stopped: Q8 holds the bus less SW1, Q7 at most the bus plus Q8's body diode
   (SLPS516 VSD 1.0 V maximum): 23.24 V.

5. THE FRONT END'S INPUT (what board E delivers into VIN_RAW)
   service 9 to 36 V (REQ-015); board E's LM5069 opens its pass FET at OVLO 37.78 / 40.09 / 42.49 V (OVLOTH 2.4 / 2.5 / 2.6 V,
   SNVS452G 6.5 p.5, over R22 100k and R23 6.65k at 1 %); the panel tracker's TRK_OUT (15.1 V) joins through an ideal
   diode; four SMCJ40A class clamps (board E D10 SMCJ40CA, D1 and D2, board A D2): VBR 44.4 to 49.1 V, VC 64.5 V at 23.3 A
   (Littelfuse, page 2 of 6). U2 regulates VBUS20 for any VIN from 4.2 to 55 V (SNVSAI1D 6.3 p.5); a line step reaches
   the bus only through the loop. MODEL, valley current mode (7.3.1) at L1 -20 %, fSW 175 kHz: the ripple rises from
   6.25 A at 36 V to 9.74 A at U2's 60 V, the average by 1.74 A until the loop answers: 0.247 V on the bus (21.207 V).
   With U2 idle Q2 blocks VIN_RAW (section 1). Above 55 V U2 leaves its recommended range and above 60 V its absolute
   ratings (VIN, VISNS, VOSNS 60 V, p.5): the clamps' 64.5 V is S-111's item; this bound assumes U2 inside its ratings.

6. CLAMPS
