10. THE SWITCH NODES: A BUDGET, NOT A BOUND (INCONCLUSIVE at desk)
   No layout exists (S-115) and no TI application note giving a layout-independent ringing bound is held. What TI does
   state: '30 V or higher voltage rating MOSFETs are preferred for 19-V to 20-V input voltage' (SLUSE66A 10.2.2.6 p.86),
   in a topology whose input loop runs through RAC with at most 10 nF + 1 nF after it (p.86, Figure 10-3 p.85), as board A
   draws it. Board A's DC band tops out 0.96 V above TI's 20 V. Board A draws R146 and R147 at 10 Ohm with C121 10 nF
   (Figure 10-3: 4.99 Ohm, CDIFF 10 nF, and CACP and CACN 33 nF to ground, p.85); without CACN, U3's ACN pin sees CH_ACN's
   ring through R146 and C121 alone. U3's VBUS pin 1 sits on VBUS20 itself.
   Budget left for ringing over the steady bus (20.96 V) and over the bound (23.40 V, INFERRED):
     Q7 VDS: the bus, Q8's VSD 1.0 V in every dead time, and SW1's ring below it; 30 V  8.04 /  5.60 V
     Q8 VDS: SW1's overshoot over the bus; 30 V                                      9.04 /  6.60 V
     U3 SW1 absolute 32 V                                                           11.04 /  8.60 V
     U3 SW1 recommended 26 V                                                         5.04 /  2.60 V
     U3 SW1 and SW2 below PGND: -2 V, and -4 V for at most 25 ns (p.8). In every dead time SW1 sits at minus Q8's VSD
     (1.0 V maximum), inside -2 V; the ring below that has 3.0 V to -4 V, for at most 25 ns
   MODEL for the layout writer (not a bound; typical driver figures, the plateau INFERRED):
   Q7's TURN-OFF (sets Q7's VDS and SW1's undershoot): its current falls in (Qgs - Qg(th)) / (VPLT / (RDS_HI_OFF + RG)) =
   1.4 nC / (2.7 V / (1.3 + 1.8 Ohm)) = 1.61 ns (SLPS526 p.3; SLUSE66A p.16); each nH of the loop C190 and C191, Q7,
   Q8 adds L x di/dt, each nH between Q8's source and U3's PGND takes SW1 that much further below minus VSD, and the
   inductance between the VBUS20 bank and C190 / C191 lifts CH_ACN by I x sqrt(L / 11 nF), which grows as the square root
   of L (the figure below is at 1 nH):
     A2, L2 peak 15.71 A:  9.77 A/ns, 9.77 V per nH and 4.74 V at 1 nH before C190; Q7's 30 V budget allows 0.82 nH;
         SW1's undershoot to -4 V (25 ns) allows 0.31 nH between Q8's source and U3's PGND
     G1, L2 peak 14.10 A:  8.77 A/ns, 8.77 V per nH and 4.25 V at 1 nH before C190; Q7's 30 V budget allows 0.92 nH;
         SW1's undershoot to -4 V (25 ns) allows 0.34 nH between Q8's source and U3's PGND
     A1, L2 peak 10.70 A:  6.66 A/ns, 6.66 V per nH and 3.23 V at 1 nH before C190; Q7's 30 V budget allows 1.21 nH;
         SW1's undershoot to -4 V (25 ns) allows 0.45 nH between Q8's source and U3's PGND
   Q7's TURN-ON (sets Q8's VDS): the current rises in 1.4 nC / ((6.0 - 2.7) V / (6.0 + 1.8 Ohm)) = 3.31 ns (the 6 Ohm
   turn-on driver, RDS_HI_ON_Q1, p.16), from the valley current; each nH adds L x di/dt:
     A2, valley 10.99 A: 3.32 A/ns, 3.32 V per nH; Q8's 30 V budget allows 2.72 nH and U3 SW1's recommended 26 V
         1.52 nH, both before the recovery below
     G1, valley  9.50 A: 2.87 A/ns, 2.87 V per nH; Q8's 30 V budget allows 3.15 nH and U3 SW1's recommended 26 V
         1.76 nH, both before the recovery below
     A1, valley  7.00 A: 2.12 A/ns, 2.12 V per nH; Q8's 30 V budget allows 4.27 nH and U3 SW1's recommended 26 V
         2.38 nH, both before the recovery below
   and Q8's body diode recovers into that edge: Qrr 8.2 nC is stated at 15 V, 18 A, 300 A/us (SLPS516 p.3), about ten times
   slower than this edge, and no figure at this di/dt is given: the recovery ring is INCONCLUSIVE, a bench reading.
   Avalanche, if a ring does pass 30 V: EAS 23 mJ (CSD17578Q5A) and 39 mJ (CSD17577Q5A), single pulse, p.1; a repetitive
   rating is not stated, so no margin is taken from it.

11. SINGLE FAULTS OUTSIDE EVERY REQUIREMENT (ASM-001 refuses 'no single point of failure'; SC-39)
   With the charger stopped Q7 and Q8 are off, L2 carries DC, and Q10's body diode (source CH_SW2, drain VBAT) holds SW2,
   and SW1 through L2, near VBAT plus a diode: Q7 then holds VBUS20 less VBAT less VSD, Q8 about VBAT plus VSD (INFERRED).
   Q2 shorted: VBUS20 = VIN_RAW less Q5's body diode (about 0.8 V, INFERRED), 35.2 V at 36 V in and 41.7 V at board E's
   OVLO maximum. On the way the bus passes ACOV's 26.0 to 27.7 V while the charger still switches (the 100 us deglitch,
   SLUSE66A p.14), and Q7 then holds the bus plus Q8's VSD, 28.7 V or more before any ringing: no order is claimed for
   that phase. Once ACOV has stopped the charger, U3's VBUS, ACP and ACN pass their 32 V absolute rating above 32.8 V in,
   while Q7 reaches 30 V only at VBUS20 = 30 V + VBAT + VSD (40.8 V with the pack at its 10.0 V CUV): from then on U3 is
   the first part past its rating while the pack is above about 1.2 V.
   R6 open or FB shorted: the OVP reads the same pin, so nothing on board A bounds the bus. The charger switches until
   ACOV trips (up to 27.7 V, after its 100 us deglitch), so Q7 holds at least 28.7 V (the trip plus Q8's VSD) while it still
   switches, before any rise inside the deglitch and before any ringing: the FETs may be first, and no order is claimed.
   Beyond, the 35 V bulk parts and U3's 32 V are passed.
   Not taken, for the power review S-111 names: an independent over-voltage trip on VBUS20 (a second divider into U34's
   channel 1, re-armed while the stage runs) would bound the FB faults; an SMCJ22A on VBUS20 (VR 22 V over the 20.96 V
   DC band) would hold a Q2 short at about 28.2 V at board E's 6.15 A hot-swap limit (INFERRED straight line) until the
   LM5069's fault timer opens, and clamps 35.5 V at its own IPP, over 30 V.

12. THE ANSWER: (a), the bound holds in service (INFERRED: it rests on a typical-only threshold)
   VBUS20 stays at or under 23.40 V by the front end's own protection whatever the load, the line or the loop model does
   while U2 is inside its ratings: Q8 6.60 V and Q7 5.60 V under their 30 V (Q7 carries Q8's VSD), U3's VBUS 8.60 V under
   its 32 V; at the INFERRED bound U3's ACOV (26.0 V minimum) is not reached. 30 V is reached only if the trip sat 36.7 %
   over VREF (Q7) or 41.5 % (Q8), against TI's typical 10 %; a bench reading of the trip replaces the INFERRED figure.
   The pack side stays at or under 20.0 V by SYSOVP and 24.27 V by D1 in a pack that opens while charging.
   The switch nodes are INCONCLUSIVE: ringing is a bench item with 8.04 V (Q7) and 9.04 V (Q8) of budget over the steady
   bus, and SW1's undershoot has 3.0 V to U3's -4 V (25 ns), carried as its own open item.
